WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.620
- So Rudy Giuliani is complaining

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.860
that the DOJ covertly got access

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:06.160
to his iCloud without notifying him.

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:07.440
And if it can happen to him,

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.700
it can happen to anyone.

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:09.533
Well yes,

00:00:09.533 --> 00:00:11.420
if the DOJ had probable cause,

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:14.370
then they can serve a warrant
on the service provider

00:00:14.370 --> 00:00:17.090
with an order that says that
they can't disclose the fact

00:00:17.090 --> 00:00:18.810
that they got access to that information,

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:19.643
or alternatively,

00:00:19.643 --> 00:00:21.080
this might not have been a search warrant.

00:00:21.080 --> 00:00:22.650
There's something called
a National Security Letter

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.200
that's an administrative subpoena

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:25.130
that doesn't give you access

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.080
to the content of something,

00:00:26.080 --> 00:00:28.820
but it does give you access
to metadata like file names

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:31.010
or subject lines for emails.

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:31.843
And yes,

00:00:31.843 --> 00:00:32.676
it's true that it's rare for

00:00:32.676 --> 00:00:33.830
the crime-fraud exception overcome

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:34.730
the attorney-client privilege

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:36.610
but that might be what's happening here.

00:00:36.610 --> 00:00:37.610
So who knows,

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.953
maybe we'll see Rudy Giuliani in court.

